      "raw": "Unlike in standard RL setups, the reward assigned to a given action in our setting depends on the model \\theta at the time the action is taken (since \\theta is updated to \\theta', which is then evaluated). As a re-sult, the underlying RL state must include the policy’s parameters and is given by (C, \\theta), even though the policy’s observation is limited to C (placing \\theta directly in context is infeasible). The implication of this is that (state, action, reward) triples collected with a previous version of the model, \\theta_{\\text{old}}, may become stale and mis-aligned for the current model \\theta_{\\text{current}}. For this reason, we adopt an on-policy approach, in which self-edits are sampled from—and, crucially, rewards are computed using—the current model.",
